      "answer": "$m=2$ at $(3,0)$; $m=-10$ at $(-3,24)$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$x^2-4x+3=mx-6\\Rightarrow x^2-x(4+m)+9=0$ — *M1. Equating and gathering terms; may be implied on the next line.\n$b^2-4ac=0\\Rightarrow(4+m)^2-4\\times9=0$ — DM1. SOI; use discriminant with their $a,b,c$.\n$4+m=\\pm6$ or $(m-2)(m+10)=0$, giving $m=2$ or $-10$ — A1. Must come from $b^2-4ac=0$ SOI.\nSubstitute both their $m$ values into their equation in line 1 — DM1.\n$m=2\\Rightarrow x=3$; $m=-10\\Rightarrow x=-3$ — A1.\n$(3,0),(-3,24)$ — A1. Accept paired statements. If final A0A0, SC B1 for one point correct WWW.\nAlternative: $\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x-4=m$ — *M1; substitute in curve/line — DM1; obtain $x=\\pm3$ — A1; obtain $y=0,24$ — A1; substitute both points to obtain $m=2,-10$ — DM1 A1. Same SC B1 condition.\nTotal: 6",
